Ticket **#4471** was filed as one known bug: the shared parser reads dates month-first while
day-first tenants write the day first. That story is true for most of the pile, but it is not
the whole pile.

The desk merged **412** unique reports into #4471. The cause logic in `#lib/kb/causes` splits
them into **two** problems that need **two** tickets.

## What #4471 actually holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The two problems

1. **`parser` — 379 reports.** The shared parser always reads month first. Day-first tenants
   (every tenant on file) get flipped days on app, email, and booking-v2 form traffic.
2. **`hint` — 33 reports.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type
   what the hint says; the form still reads the value the tenant’s day-first way. Same symptom,
   different mechanism — not fixed by the parser queue alone.

<Callout>
#4471’s page said “one issue, one fix queued.” The table above marks `hint` as not belonging
to that ticket’s owner cause. Split it out so engineering does not close the wrong half.
</Callout>

## Tickets filed

- Parser (379 reports): https://github.com/stevecookLOB/megadev/issues/1
- Hint (33 reports): https://github.com/stevecookLOB/megadev/issues/2

## Lesson

A merged count is not a single cause. Compute the groups from tenant + channel before you
call the ticket known.

